EngLawArticles.EngArticleContent:
The command of commanding officers at all levels or their authorized personnel (hereinafter referred to as "Commander"), duty officers and non-commissioned officers, shall promptly stop any individuals intruding into military installations without cause and may take the following necessary measures:
(1)Conduct the security inspections specified in Article 3, Paragraph1;
(2)Prepare a written record;
(3)Preserve evidence.
After taking the necessary measures under the preceding paragraph, if the Commander, duty officers and non-commissioned officers determine that there is no suspicion of a crime and no need for further security control of the military installation, the individual shall be ordered to leave immediately; if the individual refuses to comply, forced eviction may be carried out.
